# Cursor Execution Harness (Backend)

**Canonical:** [`../CLAUDE.md`](../CLAUDE.md) · **Backend scope:** [`CLAUDE.md`](CLAUDE.md).

> Inherits root blueprint. **`docs/DevOps/Backend/BACKEND_RULES.md`** wins on implementation detail.

---

## Before `backend/` changes

1. [`../CLAUDE.md`](../CLAUDE.md) — blueprint + agent behavior
2. [`CLAUDE.md`](CLAUDE.md) — module pathing, `apps/` siblings, hexagonal layers
3. [`docs/DevOps/Backend/BACKEND_RULES.md`](../docs/DevOps/Backend/BACKEND_RULES.md) — layers, DB, API
4. **`backend/apps/{app}/.docs/CLAUDE.md`** when editing that app (e.g. [`apps/titanic/_docs/CLAUDE.md`](apps/titanic/_docs/CLAUDE.md))

---

## Quick rules

| Item | Rule |
|------|------|
| `PYTHONPATH` | `apps` — import `titanic.*`, `core.*` (not `backend.apps.*`) |
| Entry | `main.py` — routers + middleware only |
| Run | `start-backend.ps1` → port **8000** |
| Layers | router → `dependencies/*_provider` → interactor → repository |
| `Depends` | Only in providers and routers — **not** inside interactors |
| Secrets | Never commit `backend/.env` |

---

## Sibling apps

Each peer under `apps/` (`titanic`, `audio`, `user`, …) owns hexagonal tree + optional `.docs/CLAUDE.md` + `.docs/.cursorrules`.

---

